    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d136">

                <pb facs="0231" n="129" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg129"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.918/197</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Italian Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Martino</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <p>The Italian Ambassador presents his compliments to His Excellency the Secretary
                    of State and has the honor to bring the following to his attention.</p>
                <p>The weekly paper <hi rendition="#italic">Il Martello</hi> of New York (77 East
                    10th Street) edited by the American citizen Carlo Tresca, has published under
                    the signature of Giuseppe Altieri the article here enclosed.<anchor n="7"
                        xml:id="d136-f1"/> This article contains the most vulgar and virulent attack
                    against His Majesty the King of Italy and excites its readers to the
                    assassination of the King.</p>
                <p>The Italian Ambassador feels that this publication is not only an insult to the
                    Chief of a nation which entertains the most cordial and friendly relations with
                    the United States of America, but represents a criminal activity because it is
                    beyond any doubt that encouragement to murder is a crime.</p>
                <p>The Italian Ambassador will therefore be grateful to His Excellency the Secretary
                    of State if he will inform him about the measures which, under the
                    circumstances, the American Government will think it advisable to adopt against
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Il Martello.</hi></p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1927-04-11"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">April 11, 1927</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
